                    {
                        "sense_id": "8cf0a3c9-5840-3fa6-87b1-b63793820759",
                        "entry_id": "9b59bade-2896-3bc1-abae-2583977acf9a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "физиол., мед. у теплокровных животных и человека — переохлаждение организма, понижение температуры тела из-за преобладания теплоотдачи над теплопродукцией"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dadf3bef-4f41-4bfc-ba0a-d64b0b22a8be",
                        "source_entry_id": "9b59bade-2896-3bc1-abae-2583977acf9a",
                        "source_sense_id": "8cf0a3c9-5840-3fa6-87b1-b63793820759",
                        "target_lang_word": "hypothermia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hypothermia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c84fe46-0f7b-382f-a590-7bc3f1640780",
                                        "entry_id": "b7266ae2-575d-3973-ac85-d132bfb43c07",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Abnormally low body temperature; specifically, below 35 degrees Celsius for humans."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38550773-6cb5-41ed-ba71-f29b9f4e1a60",
                                                "sense_id": "7c84fe46-0f7b-382f-a590-7bc3f1640780",
                                                "text": "Hypothermia is the systemic cold injury."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "314a448b-117e-4ebd-8d9d-9b4b176925d5",
                                                "sense_id": "7c84fe46-0f7b-382f-a590-7bc3f1640780",
                                                "text": "The stages of hypothermia begin when the body is losing heat faster than it can produce it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9783879-0b2c-4d94-866b-037cb4574f80",
                                                "sense_id": "7c84fe46-0f7b-382f-a590-7bc3f1640780",
                                                "text": "So far, extracorporeal temperature rise during COR had been limited to 20°C, as perfusion solutions had been used that were specifically designed for organ protection at hypothermia and might become inappropriate perfusates at increasing temperatures."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cacf5824-0f8c-40b1-919e-78360b8eb313",
                        "source_entry_id": "9b59bade-2896-3bc1-abae-2583977acf9a",
                        "source_sense_id": "8cf0a3c9-5840-3fa6-87b1-b63793820759",
                        "target_lang_word": "hipotermia",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hipotermia",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4d9699f5-71bb-3f99-bb17-c499e654897c",
                                        "entry_id": "9d2cd6dd-8c70-3521-a37f-9e360a14a2e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Descenso involuntario de la temperatura corporal por debajo de 35 °C medida con termómetro en el recto o el esófago."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Patologías"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd7fb39a-be51-4fb1-b0c0-bd2060c853de",
                                                "sense_id": "4d9699f5-71bb-3f99-bb17-c499e654897c",
                                                "text": "«En el tiempo que tenía, comí algo de queso y después fui a bañarme. El agua estaba demasiado fría y tenía mucha pereza como para ir a encender la caldera, así que me arriesgué a morir de hipotermia»."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "213615ee-e30e-47cb-9165-f83599845683",
                        "source_entry_id": "9b59bade-2896-3bc1-abae-2583977acf9a",
                        "source_sense_id": "8cf0a3c9-5840-3fa6-87b1-b63793820759",
                        "target_lang_word": "ipotermia",
                        "target_lang_code": "it",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
